      "body": "After the first sync, the app keeps your data **on the device**. With no signal you keep creating, checking, editing and working out. When the connection returns, everything goes up on its own, in the order you did it.\n\n## The sync dot\n\n- **Green** — all caught up\n- **Yellow** — sending or receiving\n- **Red** — offline (what you do is kept) or something was refused; open it to see which\n\nTap it (or Profile → Sync) to see the queue and force a send.\n\n## Server unavailable\n\nIf the server is down (maintenance, outage), the dot says **Server unavailable** and you **stay signed in**, using what is on the device, even after closing and reopening the app. When the server is back, the app renews access and sends what was kept, without asking you to sign in. It only asks you to sign in again when the server itself ends the session (password changed, session ended elsewhere), and the sign-in screen tells you why.\n\n## Conflicts\n\nIf you and someone else change the same task offline, the last change **for each field** wins. For the description, the losing version is kept: \"See previous version\" shows up.\n\n## What needs a connection\n\nInvites, the students panel, automations, reports and the shop."
